        "at-0001": "Round money only with round_money Always round monetary Decimal results with ledgerly.money.round_money (half-up to the cent); never use Python's round() or a bare Decimal.quantize(), which use banker's rounding and produce wrong invoice totals.",
        "at-0002": "Raise BillingError with machine-readable codes Reject invalid input by raising BillingError(code, detail) from ledgerly.errors, using short snake_case codes like \"invalid_state\", \"invalid_quantity\" and \"negative_amount\"; never raise bare ValueError.",
